# B0 (no card opened): build the window image tp4-u1-1 from the pushed tp4/u1 commit. The profile named is the production default; nothing is baked as the image default
# (no C2_BAKE_DEFAULT_PROFILE), so the image default stays qwen_c2_profiles.json's c2-packed-tp4. THE TAG MUST BE FRESH: the build step skips a tag that already exists.
# The image differs from tp4-262k8-best-1 in host Python only (tile_collective_tp.py, packed_verifier.py, c2_smoke_check.py, the two U1 profiles): no graft .so, no kernel. Every result of the window is UNQUALIFIED (the 262k evidence waiver of the gate-only arms).
# READ: the build log's provenance report with no problem line, the closure checks pass, the image id printed. Never run it during a timing job. Duration (estimate): 20-60 min. Stop rule: a build or provenance failure stops the window.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/u1 development window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/u1 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-u1-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/u1 commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=build
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-u1-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4
